# Project description

We want to create an Android App to login to a server using DHIS2 Android SDK (https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-android-sdk), if the login is succesfull, reach to a home page saying hello username, if it has a login error, show the error in a toast.

For login with the SDK please follow this snippet:

d2.userModule().logIn(username, password, serverUrl)

more info: https://developers.dhis2.org/docs/mobile/android-sdk/workflow

# Tech stack
- For the ui use the compose multiplatform DHIS2 design system (https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-mobile-ui), if there is a component that you need and is not in the library, please use compose multiplatform, and if not, use material 3. Please don't use xml for the UI.

- The architecture should be simple, using ViewModel to interact with the UI. The ViewModels will know a repository interface which will have an impletation to use the DHIS2 Android SDK and abstract the framework to the domain. For architectura best practices reference: https://developer.android.com/topic/architecture

- For dependency injection use Koin.
